  "classIri": "urn:ngm:class:vesting-schedule",
  "domain": "blockchain",
  "definition": "A vesting schedule is a contractually or programmatically enforced timetable that releases allocated digital assets or equity to recipients incrementally over a defined period, typically beginning after an initial cliff during which no release occurs. In blockchain and token-based systems, schedules are commonly encoded in smart contracts that autonomously unlock portions of a token allocation at fixed intervals or milestones, aligning the long-term incentives of founders, contributors, and investors with project health. The schedule's parameters \u2014 cliff length, total duration, release cadence, and revocation conditions \u2014 are a principal instrument of tokenomics design and governance risk management.",
